# BRIEF B1997 | SEAT-X56: OXPd 2 KICK-OFF, LANE L5 (THE OLDER PRINTER'S FIRST LAB READ): THE LAB COMMAND `oxpd1` WITH TWO VERBS. `oxpd1 read` FETCHES THE DISCOVERY TREE AND MAKES ONE READ WITH THE ADMIN PASSWORD OVER THE LANDED OXPd 1.x CLIENT (FIRST-RUN STEP 1), PINNED, WITH A FIRST CONTACT THROUGH THE LAB'S OWN CHANNEL; THE PASSWORD IS SENT AT MOST ONCE PER RUN AND ANY REFUSAL STOPS THE RUN; IT IS READ FROM A CREDENTIALS FILE ONLY. `--addressing 2005|2004` IS THE ONE SWITCH BETWEEN THE TWO WS-ADDRESSING VERSIONS (A NEW `Oxpd1ClientOptions.Addressing`). `oxpd1 lab-cert` MAKES A DEVELOPMENT CA AND A SERVER CERTIFICATE FOR A HOST NAME, NEVER AN IP ADDRESS, AND KEEPS NO CA KEY. BOTH REFUSE A RUN FOLDER INSIDE A GIT WORK TREE. LANDS AFTER LANE L4 (`print`). 12 NEW LAB CELLS (32 CASES) AND 2 CLIENT CELLS (4 CASES) AGAINST A STUB ON 127.0.0.1; RED FIRST: 16 CASES RED ON A PERMISSIVE FIRST SHAPE, 15 MUTANTS. ONE COMMIT ON A NEW BRANCH IN YOUR OWN CLONE, PUSHED, THE FOUR HOSTED CHECKS GREEN, ENDING AT `READY B1997: <sha40>` WITH NO PULL REQUEST. NO CONNECTION TO ANY PRINTER OR DEVICE, NO WRITE TO ANY DEVICE, NO TRUST STORE, NO slnx LINE, NO PACKAGE, NO WORKFLOW CHANGE, NO JIRA CALL, NO AZURE, NOTHING TO HP OR ANY PERSON, NO SPEND.

**Purpose and generation (the commission's lines 6 to 12, RELAYED; B1968's needs list section 2a, read by the drafter):** both verbs are for an OXPd 1.x (FutureSmart 5) device, which is what the product owner's HP Color LaserJet MFP M577 is (B1968 section 4, RELAYED). `oxpd1 read` is step 1 of the first-run list ("DeviceInfo over OXPd (port 7627) with the admin password: model, firmware, OXPd version", B1968 line 65) and keeps that list's guard ("five wrong admin passwords lock the account ... so the tool stops after one authentication failure", B1968 line 72). `oxpd1 lab-cert` makes what steps 3 to 5 need before they can work: an OXPd 1.x device refuses a server named by an IP address (design review B1996 F7, line 54, citing `C1:93`), so the lab server needs a host name and a certificate for it. **This lane connects to nothing: every cell runs against a stub on 127.0.0.1 inside the test process; `lab-cert` opens no connection at all.** Neither verb can reach an OXPd 2 (FutureSmart 6) device's services: the SOAP reads exist only on OXPd 1.x (DERIVED from the client's README line 1). What the M577 answers, which addressing version it accepts, which certificates it presents on 7627 and 443, and how it resolves a host name are UNMEASURED.

