## THE DECISIONS OF THIS COMMIT (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp)
- **D1: one command, two verbs, one table line, after L4's.** `oxpd1 read` and `oxpd1 lab-cert` live in ONE folder `src/Datasec.Suite.Lab/Commands/Oxpd1/` behind ONE `ILabCommand`, so the command table gains exactly one line (`new Oxpd1.Oxpd1Command(),` at `CommandRegistry.cs:27`, after L4's line). Two landed cells pin the table's names exactly: P13 (`ProbeTests.cs:207`, `["probe", "print"]` on the L4 TREE) and L4's R11 (`Print/PrintTests.cs:188`, the same list): any new command reddens both (MEASURED on the L4 TREE, `<d>/logs/q-exe-lab.log`: R11 `Assert.Equal() Failure: Collections differ`; on `d804de5e` P13 likewise), so each list becomes `["probe", "print", "oxpd1"]`, one line out and one in each (Q10). The command's documentation is its own `README.md` in the folder, and ONE entry of four lines in the Lab README, after L4's `print` entry.
- **D2: no fifth copy of the pin rule.** First contact: the Lab's `DeviceChannel` with no pin (one GET planned per port, refused at the handshake; `ReadOnlyRule` admits it; the channel records it in the run folder). Pinned read: the client's own check through `PinnedCertificateSha256` (at most two pins: 7627 and 443 may present different certificates). The client has no seam that takes a check from outside; adding one would change the client's trust code, which this lane does not own beyond the addressing switch (Q2).
- **D3: ONE password-bearing request per run, structurally.** The command calls `ReadAsync` exactly once (`Oxpd1Command.cs:312`); the discovery tree before it carries no `Authorization` header (the client's `GetDiscoveryTreeAsync`, `Oxpd1Client.cs:65`, sends none); every end of the read ends the run. A 401 or 403 (HP's "missing" and "invalid" credentials, `Oxpd1ReadResult.cs:17` and `:20`) prints a line holding `authentication failed` and `five failed attempts lock` and exits 6; a fault, another status, a malformed answer, a time-out or no connection exits 8. The count is per run (Q3).
- **D4: the password from a credentials file only**, read by name: the line `<name>=<value>` (one pair of matching quotes dropped), name `OXPD_TEST_PRINTER_ADMIN_PASSWORD` unless `--password-name` gives another (B1968 line 38's proposed name). MEASURED at `d804de5e` (`<d>/scratch/evidence/base-prior-control.txt`): the Lab project reads NO secret today (a `git grep -c -i -E` over `src` for `GetEnvironmentVariable`, `.env` and `credentials file`: rc 1, no line; control `readSetting` 7 in the client), so "as the Lab project already reads secrets" has nothing to reuse; the file reader is this lane's (`LabFiles.cs:15`). The environment is not read (cell L03 counts `Environment.` 0 in the folder). The path is given on the command line; the value never is (Q4).
- **D5: the WS-Addressing switch is a client option** (`Oxpd1ClientOptions.Addressing`, a new public enum `Oxpd1Addressing` with `Version200508` (default) and `Version200408`, an undefined value refused): the envelope writes the same four headers in `http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2004/08/addressing` with `ReplyTo` `.../role/anonymous` (the 2004 submission's anonymous address: DERIVED from that specification's text, not from any committed HP file; UNMEASURED on a device). The landed contract cell C07 (the namespace sent by default equals the bindings') is unchanged and stays green (MEASURED).
- **D6: `lab-cert` keeps no CA key.** RSA 2048 with SHA-256; the CA (basic constraints CA, path length 0, certificate signing) signs one server certificate and its key object is disposed unwritten; `server.crt` carries the host name as subject and as its ONLY alternative name, server authentication, not a CA; validity `--days` (1 to 397, default 30). A second certificate needs a new CA and a new upload to the device (Q5).
- **D7: run records stay out of git by a refusal, not by an ignore line.** Both verbs refuse a run folder that is inside a git work tree (a `.git` folder or file in it or above it), exit 9, before anything is written. A `.gitignore` line would be a shared root file outside this lane (Q6). The probe's own run folder is not changed (L1's file; a limit).
- **D8: the key file's mode** is owner read and write only on macOS and Linux (`UnixCreateMode`); Windows has no such mode, so cell L01 asserts it only where `OperatingSystem.IsWindows()` is false. This is a designed platform branch of the CODE, not a cell made platform-aware in answer to a red.
- **D9: ONE commit, on a new branch from BASE (main after L4); the rebase rule before the first push only** (SHARED FILES AND MAIN).

## THE REQUIRED SECTION: what is each verb handed that is NOT the tested shape?
**The properties (each a behaviour sentence this lane freezes; the paths named are the only writers and callers, found by `grep -n` over the folder at the head):** (P1) on every run of `oxpd1 read`, at most ONE request carries the admin password, it is sent only after the credentials file gave a value and the discovery tree read ended in anything but a pin refusal, and every end of it ends the run (`Oxpd1Command.cs` `PinnedReadAsync`, the only caller of `ReadAsync`); (P2) the password is never taken from the command line and never printed, summarised or recorded (`Oxpd1Command.cs` `Parse`, the `lines` list, `RunRecorder.Summary`, the client's record file); (P3) no run folder inside a git work tree is created (`RunFolderRule.GitWorkTreeHolding`, called by both verbs before `RunRecorder.Create`); (P4) neither verb writes to a device (the five reads are the client's closed list; `--read` takes only a defined name starting `Get`; `lab-cert` opens no connection); (P5) `lab-cert` names the server by a host name only and writes no CA key; (P6) the addressing version sent is the one asked for, 2005 by default. **At least these shapes; any other shape you meet: name it in STATUS with its cell or a named limit, never leave it out, and add no cell beyond the patch.** The commission's item 11 asks for three shapes NOT the tested shape per property: P1 has H4, H5, H6; P2 has H8, H9, H10; P3 has H12, H13, H14; P5 has H16, H17, H18.
| # | Shape | Cell, mutant or named limit |
|---|---|---|
| H1 | **the right pin, an answer** | R02: exactly `GET /DevMgmt/DiscoveryTree.xml` (no `Authorization`) then `POST /hp/device/webservices/OXPd/DeviceInfoService`; exactly 1 request carries HTTP Basic for `admin` with the synthetic password (`Oxpd1Stub.CarryingPassword`); the password in no output and no file of the run folder; `mEveryRead` |
| H2 | **401, 403, a SOAP fault (500)** | R03 (3 cases): exit 6, 6, 8; exactly 1 password-bearing request, 1 request with any `Authorization`, 2 requests in all; the lockout message; `mRetryOn401`, `mStopIgnored`, `mEveryRead` |
| H3 | **no pin: first contact** | R01: exit 3, the stub's SHA-256 printed with `--pin <sha>`, 0 requests, the handshake reached the stub (the lab channel's landed cells P01 and P04 cover the same check) |
| H4 | **the HTTP layer resending the password request** (a pooled connection reused) | NO CELL; a named limit, DERIVED: the SOAP port's first request opens a new connection (the tree is on another port in a real run); in the cells both ports are the stub's one port, and R02/R03 count exactly 1 password-bearing request, so no resend happened on the paths the cells cover |
| H5 | **a 401 carrying a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge** | NO CELL; a named limit, DERIVED: the client never sets `Credentials` on its handler (`Oxpd1Client.cs:43-51`), so the handler answers no challenge; the stub's 401 carries no challenge header |
| H6 | **a second run, or two runs at once** | NO CELL; a named limit (D3, Q3): the count is per run; across runs and callers it belongs to the shared device-trust component (B1996 F16) |
| H7 | **no value: a missing file, another name, an empty value** | R05 (3 cases): exit 7, "nothing was sent", 0 TLS connections; `mCredentialLate` |
| H8 | **`--password <value>`, `--admin-password <value>`, no `--credentials-file`** | R06 (3 cases): exit 2, 0 TLS connections, the value not in the output, the usage line holds `--password-name ` and no `--password `; `mPasswordOption` |
| H9 | **the password echoed in an answer** | the client's masking (its landed cells K12 and the README's "What it holds to"); R02's whole-run-folder search covers the stub's answer, which holds no password; a named limit beyond the client's cells |
| H10 | **a credentials line written `export NAME=value`, with spaces around `=`, or two lines of the name** | NO CELL; a named limit: an `export` or spaced line is not read (the run ends exit 7, nothing sent); the FIRST line of the name wins (`LabFiles.cs:28` to `:39`) |
| H11 | **a read that is not one of the five; a case variant** | R09 (4 cases): `GetSignInMethods` and `GetAuthenticationAgentRecords` go to their services with 1 password-bearing request; `SetSignInMethods` and `getmanufacturerinfo` exit 2 with 0 connections; `mEveryRead` |
| H12 | **a `.git` folder above the run folder; a `.git` FILE (a linked work tree or submodule)** | R07 (5 cases, both verbs, with the no-`.git` control): exit 9, the run folder not created, 0 TLS connections; `mGitIgnored`, `mGitFileIgnored` |
| H13 | **a run folder reached through a symbolic link into a work tree** | NO CELL; a named limit: `Path.GetFullPath` does not resolve links, so a link outside any work tree that points into one is not refused |
| H14 | **a work tree named by `GIT_DIR` or `GIT_WORK_TREE` only (no `.git` entry)** | NO CELL; a named limit: the check reads the file system only and no environment |
| H15 | **the addressing option: none, `2005`, `2004`; an undefined enum value** | R08 (3 cases): the stub saw the Action header in the asked namespace and `ReplyTo` its anonymous address; A01 (3 cases): the four headers in that namespace and none in the other, `mustUnderstand="1"` on Action and To; A02: the default and a refused `(Oxpd1Addressing)7`; `mAddressingDropped`, `mSeamIgnored` |
| H16 | **an IPv4 or IPv6 address, a wildcard, a trailing dot, `localhost`, a port** | L02 (6 cases): exit 2, the run folder not created; `mIpAccepted` |
| H17 | **a CA key kept, or a key in the certificate file** | L01: exactly four files, `server.key` the only one holding `PRIVATE KEY`, `ca.crt` loads with no key; `mKeyInCertFile` |
| H18 | **a name the certificate does not carry; an IP address against it** | L01: `MatchesHostname` true for the name, false for another name and for `127.0.0.1`; the alternative names exactly the one DNS name and no IP address; `mNoSan` |
| H19 | **the server certificate's chain, use and validity** | L01: chain builds to `ca.crt` only (control: another CA fails), server authentication only, not a CA, CA flag on the CA, about 7 days for `--days 7`; `mNoEku` |
| H20 | **the key file readable by others** | L01 (macOS and Linux): mode owner read and write only; `mKeyModeOpen` |
| H21 | **a trust store, a started program, an environment read** | L03: the folder's three `.cs` files hold no `X509Store`, `Process` or `Environment.` (control: `CertificateRequest` found); `mStoreNamed`; `checks_l5.py` check 7 over the added `src/` lines |
| H22 | **a real device: its certificates, its answer, its addressing, its name resolution, its acceptance of the certificate** | NEVER in this lane; a named limit: all UNMEASURED; no cell makes a TLS handshake with the written certificate files |
| H23 | **any shape you meet that is not above** | a named limit in STATUS (no new cell) |
**Platform behaviour:** the subject of R01 to R09 is the platform's TLS and HTTP stack against a Kestrel TLS stub; the landed Lab cells already run such a stub on both hosted legs (`StubDevice.cs:118`, `UseHttps`). L01's subject includes the platform's X.509 code (`CreateFromPemFile`, `X509Chain` with a custom root, `MatchesHostname`) and, off Windows, `UnixFileMode`. The drafter ran macOS arm64 only. Legs that can show a red: your macOS run, the hosted `linux` leg and the hosted `windows` leg. **If ONE leg alone is red (green on the others), that is `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <leg> red alone on <cell> with its message`: never a skipped cell, a platform-aware cell, a retry or a re-run.**

